# Key Value Contract for the AV clock.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE CONTRACT for what this component measures. A vendor
# implements against the description on each key; a test suite asserts against
# it. AFTER EDITING, RUN: scripts/kvcc.py
#
# This vocabulary sits BESIDE the interface versions, never inside one, so a
# revision here moves no frozen interface hash.
#
# A key absent here is ABSENT at runtime — never 0, never -1. unit and kind are
# part of a key's identity. A counter is monotonic from resource creation and is
# never reset on open(), flush(), stop() or seek.
#
# SIGN IS MEANINGFUL ON THIS ELEMENT. sync_offset_ms is positive when audio
# leads and negative when video leads: they are opposite directions of one
# measurement, so the value is signed int64 and a reader must not treat it as a
# magnitude. This is also why no key here can carry a -1 sentinel — it would be
# indistinguishable from a legitimate one-millisecond offset.

format: kvc
schema: 1

domain: av
component: clock
package: avclock
version: 1.0

instances: 1

captureCadenceMs: 50

keys:

  # av.clock.sync_offset_ms
  - name: sync_offset_ms
    type: int64
    unit: ms
    kind: current
    access: read
    provider: driver
    description: >
      The driver's predicted current audio-versus-video presentation offset.
      Positive when audio leads, negative when video leads. A live sample rather
      than a cumulative figure.

  # av.clock.sync_max_abs_offset_ms
  - name: sync_max_abs_offset_ms
    type: int64
    unit: ms
    kind: high_water
    access: read
    provider: driver
    description: >
      Largest absolute sync_offset_ms observed. A monotone non-decreasing
      high-water mark over the life of the resource, and read-only: a maximum
      cannot be recovered by differencing two maxima, so a consumer wanting the
      worst excursion within its own reporting window tracks that itself from
      sync_offset_ms rather than resetting a figure other readers share.

  # av.clock.sync_time_over_threshold_ms
  - name: sync_time_over_threshold_ms
    type: int64
    unit: ms
    kind: counter
    access: read
    provider: driver
    description: >
      Cumulative time the absolute sync_offset_ms exceeded sync_threshold_ms —
      the time integral of out-of-sync operation.

  # av.clock.sync_threshold_ms
  - name: sync_threshold_ms
    type: int64
    unit: ms
    kind: config
    access: read
    provider: driver
    description: >
      The offset magnitude beyond which playback counts as out of sync. This is
      the threshold sync_time_over_threshold_ms integrates against and
      sync_max_abs_offset_ms is judged by, so declaring either of those without
      this leaves both uninterpretable — reading it is what the key is for. The
      value is set by product configuration rather than over this interface, so
      a consumer never has to assume the threshold it was built against is the
      one in force.

  # av.clock.resync_count
  - name: resync_count
    type: int64
    unit: events
    kind: counter
    access: read
    provider: driver
    description: >
      Count of A/V-sync corrections the clock applied, one per discrete
      realignment of audio and video.

  # av.clock.resync_magnitude_sum_ms
  - name: resync_magnitude_sum_ms
    type: int64
    unit: ms
    kind: counter
    access: read
    provider: driver
    description: >
      Sum of the absolute magnitude of each resync correction. Clock-internal,
      and paired with resync_count so the mean correction size is this divided
      by that.
